  "question": {
    "text": "A diatomic molecule is made of two masses $m_1$ and $m_2$ which are separated by a distance $r$. If we calculate its rotational energy by applying Bohr's rule of angular momentum quantization, its energy will be given by ( $n$ is an integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AeD11",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\left(m_1+m_2\\right)^2 n^2 h^2}{2 m_1^2 m_2^2 r^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "W40sI",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{n^2 h^2}{2\\left(m_1+m_2\\right) r^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
